{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UvRNX9yRxG5vU2zpD6iYbc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tid: 6a623e28-418d-43c9-96dc-2f53fb4ca03b\n3\tslug: oxygen-tank-2\n4\tname: \"Oxygen tank No. 2\"\n5\ttype: topic\n6\tdescription: Apollo 13 service module tank whose 28-volt thermostatic switches failed under 65-volt power and caused the explosion\n7\tcreated: 2026-10-24\n8\tupdated: 2026-10-24\n9\taliases: [\"oxygen tank No. 2\", \"O2 tank 2\", \"oxygen tank 2\"]\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Facts\n13\t\n14\t- [stated] Exploded on 1970-04-13, about 56 hours into the flight (src: NASA Apollo 13 mission page, 2026-10-24)\n15\t- [stated] Its thermostatic switches were built to a 1962 specification for 28 volts DC (src: Moonport SP-4204, 2026-10-24)\n16\t- [stated] The heater specification was revised in 1965 to 65 volts but the switches were not changed (src: Moonport SP-4204, 2026-10-24)\n17\t- [stated] Before launch it was emptied by running its heaters on 65-volt ground power for about eight hours (src: Moonport SP-4204, 2026-10-24)\n18\t\n19\t## Links\n20\t\n21\t- carried by [[command-service-module]]\n22\t- built by [[beech-aircraft]]\n23\t- crippled [[apollo-13]]\n24\t- examined by [[apollo-13-review-board]]\n25\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be057c44-3b64-4907-a6cd-bd3797d41460","uuid":"0454ea9e-6143-482b-8598-d16f47700429","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:15:32.280Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\shman\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-shman-OneDrive-Desktop-Yggdrass-OS-Yggdrass-OS\\4def6ebb-4bae-4ed4-85d0-92ed32e7bd0c\\scratchpad\\exp7\\brain-B\\topics\\oxygen-tank-2.md","content":"---\nid: 6a623e28-418d-43c9-96dc-2f53fb4ca03b\nslug: oxygen-tank-2\nname: \"Oxygen tank No. 2\"\ntype: topic\ndescription: Apollo 13 service module tank whose 28-volt thermostatic switches failed under 65-volt power and caused the explosion\ncreated: 2026-10-24\nupdated: 2026-10-24\naliases: [\"oxyge