{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRYNjHbwX2CDPwSgVote","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ANSWER: Edgar Cortright chaired the board while he was director of NASA's Langley Research Center. The board traced the explosion to an electrically started fire in oxygen tank No. 2. The cause was its thermostatic switches, which were built to a 1962 spec for 28 volts DC. The heater spec was revised in 1965 to 65 volts, but the switches were not changed. The board called this a serious oversight that all parties shared, and recommended removing all electrical equipment from inside the tank.\n\nFILES:\n- areas/apollo-13-review-board.md\n- sources/apollo-13-review-board-report.md\n- areas/apollo-13.md\n- topics/oxygen-tank-2.md\n- people/edgar-cortright.md"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":588,"cache_read_input_tokens":28135,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":588,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be057c44-3b64-4907-a6cd-bd3797d41460","uuid":"46c67969-c204-46c0-ba0a-f3f0433793e3","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:15:37.127Z","request_id":"req_011CgRYNiuH6BdYZM3raVt4a"}
